# Local / build artifacts (not part of the deployed site)
# .claude is dropped except the one skill the build checks (see below).
.git
.claude/*
!.claude/skills
node_modules
dist
screenshots
art_templates
instagram
# Anchor to repo root: a bare "motion" also matches public/media/motion/,
# which holds the essays' referenced .mp4 files and must stay deployed.
/motion
threads-backup-*.json
*.md
# The prebuild documentation test reads this file; it is build input, not a
# public asset. Keep the test and include its input in Vercel's filtered tree.
!CLAUDE.md
# The prebuild connector test rebuilds the Living Brand connector and compares
# it, and the project copy of its skill, with what is committed. Both skill
# files are build input in the same way; neither is served.
!living-brand/skills/living-brand/SKILL.md
!.claude/skills/living-brand/SKILL.md

# Unserved source/cache media (verified: not referenced anywhere in src/).
# NOTE: keep public/media/drawings (its full/ + thumbs/ web versions ARE served);
# only the raw .tif sources there are dropped via the *.tif rule below.
public/media/cache
public/images/case-studies/PORTO ROCHA - Gemini
public/images/case-studies/Workbench/workbench_architecture

# Raw source asset types never referenced by the site
*.tif
*.tiff
*.wav
*.psd
*.ai

# Experiment entries are the SOURCE for the generated /experiments pages, so
# they have to survive the blanket "*.md" rule above — the build reads them.
!content/experiments/*.md
